# Build outputs and transient PyInstaller state — regenerated by
# build-release.ps1, never committed.
# Exception: payload/management/ (Parkos.psd1/.psm1/about_Parkos.help.txt) is
# first-party, versioned source, NOT a downloaded/build artifact - Get-ManagementModulePayload
# in build-release.ps1 validates it exists in the repo instead of fetching it.
# Exception: payload/README-EULA.txt is the End-User License Agreement - first-party
# legal document, not a build artifact. Show-Eula in parkos-installer.ps1 requires
# it to be present at install time (resolves via $script:PayloadRoot/README-EULA.txt).
payload/*
!payload/management/
!payload/README-EULA.txt
# Exception: payload/postgres/ holds the Postgres 16 Windows binaries split in
# ~83 MB parts (GitHub rejects single files > 100 MB) plus the SHA-256 of the
# whole zip. The installers reassemble and verify them. The reassembled .zip
# (332 MB) must NEVER be committed; neither must payload/security/parkos-master.key
# (it stays ignored by payload/*).
!payload/postgres/
payload/postgres/*.zip
.pyinstaller-work/
__pycache__/
*.spec
